  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies quantum circuit Born machines with tensor-network pretraining and metric-based circuit extension on two simulation-only benchmarks: a 9-qubit 3x3 Bars-and-Stripes dataset and a 12-qubit Japanese government bond interest-rate dataset. On BAS, the metric-based extension uses 10 added connections and outperforms random and linear baselines on test MMD, while on JGB it adds 13 new connections (21 total) and improves train MMD over linear and random extensions; no classical advantage is demonstrated.",
